--TEST--
`Core\Http::methodName` takes a `Core\Http\Method` case and nothing else, so text naming a verb does not compile — `rule:enums/closed-integer-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The member turns a case into text and never the reverse: a string is not a
// case, so the call is refused before the program runs.
echo Core\Http::methodName("GET"), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Http\Method`, found `string`
  --> case.nvs:4:28
%A
